  "prefLabel": "En 801.01 Purpose",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 801.01 Purpose.\n\n(a) The purpose of En 800 is to protect the public, operators, and excavators from physical harm, damages, and interrupted service resulting from damage to underground facilities.\n\n(b) En 800 establishes procedures and requirements relative to:\n\n(1) Minimum requirements for the operation of the system, including notification procedures;\n\n(2) The investigation of complaints including enforcement;\n\n(3) Emergency situations for which notice of excavation pursuant to RSA 374:51, II, is not required; and\n\n(4) Minimum standards of marking the tolerance zone.\n\nSource. #14062, eff 8-21-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en800.html"
